@startuml
!include style.puml
title The public API surface (stewart-php/contracts)

interface App {
    +initialize(): void
}

interface Disposable {
    +dispose(): void
}

interface HaContext {
    .. reads — never suspend ..
    +getState(id): ?EntityState
    +getEntity(id): Entity
    +requireState(id): EntityState
    +listStates(selector): EntityStateCollection
    .. streams ..
    +watchStateChanges(selector): StateChangeStream
    +watchEvents(eventType): EventStream
    +watchTopic(pattern): EventStream
    +watchConnection(): EventStream
    .. actions — suspend ..
    +callAction(action, data, target): EventContext
    +callActionForResponse(action, data, target): ServiceResponse
    +fireEvent(type, data): EventContext
    +getHistory(id, query): EntityStateHistory
    +waitForState(id, state, timeout): ?EntityState
    +publish(topic, payload): void
    +isConnected(): bool
}

interface "EventStream<T>" as Stream {
    +subscribe(Closure): Subscription
    .. operators — worker-side ..
    +filter(predicate): static
    +map(fn): EventStream
    +debounce(Duration, Edge): static
    +throttle(Duration, Edge): static
    +take(n): static
    +takeUntil(EventStream): static
}

interface "StateChangeStream" as ChangeStream {
    .. Home Assistant shaped, per entity ..
    +distinctUntilChanged(): static
    +whenChangedTo(state, for, from, fromAnyState): static
    +whenStableFor(Duration): static
    +whenAbove(threshold, for): static
    +whenBelow(threshold, for): static
    +startWithCurrentState(): static
    +acrossEntities(): EventStream
}

interface Timers {
    +startTimer(Duration, Closure): TimerHandle
}

interface Scheduler {
    +runEvery(Duration, Closure): ScheduledTask
    +runDailyAt(TimeOfDay, Closure, DayOfWeek...): ScheduledTask
    +runOnCron(expression, Closure): ScheduledTask
    +runAfter(Duration, Closure): ScheduledTask
    +runAt(DateTimeImmutable, Closure): ScheduledTask
    +runAtSunEvent(SunEvent, Closure, SunOffset): ScheduledTask
    +runAtEntityTime(entity, Closure): ScheduledTask
}

interface Schedule {
    +findNextOccurrenceAfter(DateTimeImmutable): ?DateTimeImmutable
    +describe(): string
}

interface ScheduledTask {
    +cancel(): void
    +isActive(): bool
    +getNextRunAt(): ?Instant
    +getId(): string
}

Stream <|-- ChangeStream

interface Subscription {
    +unsubscribe(): void
    +isActive(): bool
    +getId(): string
}

class Selector <<final>> {
    +getKind(): SelectorKind
    +getPattern(): string
    +listMembers(): SelectorCollection
    +{static} exact(), glob(), regex(), anyOf(), any(), fromSpec()
    +matches(candidate): bool
    +toCanonicalKey(): string
    +findExactPattern(): ?string
}

enum SelectorKind {
    Exact
    Glob
    Regex
    AnyOf
}

class EntityState {
    +entityId, state
    +attributes[]
    +getDomain(), isUnavailable()
    +getStateAsFloat(), get*Attribute()
}
class StateChange {
    +from, to  (both nullable)
    +hasStateChanged()
    +changedTo(state)
    +changedFrom(state)
}

App .left. Disposable : an app may also implement
App -right-> HaContext : constructed with
App ..> Scheduler : constructed with
Scheduler ..> Schedule : accepts
Scheduler ..> ScheduledTask : returns
HaContext --> Stream : returns
HaContext ..> EntityState : returns
Stream --> Subscription : returns
Stream ..> StateChange : yields
HaContext ..> Selector : accepts

Selector --> SelectorKind

note bottom of Selector
  **Value objects**, never closures.
  An event or topic selector crosses to the broker
  as JSON and routes there; every predicate and
  operator runs worker-side. A string is exact or
  a glob; a regex is only built on request.
end note

note right of Stream
  A stream rather than a bare callback, so the
  operator layer landed without changing a single
  existing call site. Each operator is a decorator;
  nothing registers until subscribe().
end note

note right of ChangeStream
  Every operator that keeps the element type hands
  back a StateChangeStream, so whenChangedTo() still
  chains after a filter(). Only map() drops out.
end note

note right of Timers
  Timers are a port: Revolt in the runtime, a virtual
  clock in tests. It is what lets debounce and the
  scheduler be tested with no event loop.
end note

note right of Scheduler
  Injected beside HaContext, not hung off it: operators
  compose over an event source, and a schedule has none.
  Occurrences resolve in Home Assistant's timezone.
end note
@enduml
